        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({\n  generationConfig: { temperature: 0.3, topP: 0.95, topK: 40, maxOutputTokens: 1024, responseMimeType: 'application/json' },\n  contents: [{ role: 'user', parts: [{ text: `Write the owner's daily summary for an outbound research system. Three to five sentences, plain English, for someone reading on a phone.\n\nYou are given exact counts. Use those numbers and only those numbers. Never state a figure that is not supplied to you.\n\nIf anything failed, lead with that. Good news never goes before bad news.\nIf nothing was due today, say so plainly and state what is still active. Never send an empty or apologetic summary.\nNever write an em dash or en dash.\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON, no fences:\n{ \"subject\": \"\", \"summary\": \"\", \"has_failures\": true or false }\n\nTODAY'S NUMBERS:\n- Follow ups drafted: ${ $('M7 Gmail Draft follow up').isExecuted ? $('M7 Gmail Draft follow up').all().filter(i => !i.json.error).length : 0 }\n- Sequences stopped because the prospect replied: ${ $('M6a stop sequence replied').isExecuted ? $('M6a stop sequence replied').all().length : 0 }, domains: ${ $('M6a stop sequence replied').isExecuted ? ($('M6a stop sequence replied').all().map(i => i.json.domain).join(', ') || 'none') : 'none' }\n- Failures: ${ $('M7 Gmail Draft follow up').isExecuted ? ($('M7 Gmail Draft follow up').all().filter(i => i.json.error).map(i => i.json.domain || 'a follow up').join(', ') || 'none') : 'none' }\n- Sequences still active: ${ $('M2 sequence_queue queued').all().filter(r => r.json.queue_id).length }` }] }]\n}) }}",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 60000
        }
